          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Gopakumar-Vafa invariants are supposed to count the number of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudoholomorphic+curves"} pseudoholomorphic curves
            and represent the number of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+states"} BPS states
            on a three-dimensional projective
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+manifold"} Calabi-Yau manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rajesh+Gopakumar"} Rajesh Gopakumar
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
            first described the invariant in (
            %a{:href => "#GopakumarVafa98a"}> GV 98a
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GopakumarVafa98b"} GV 98b
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GopakumarVafa98c"} GV 98c
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#GopakumarVafa99"} GV 99
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gromov-Witten+invariants"} Gromov-Witten invariants
            and Pandharipande-Thomas invariants also count the numbers of holomorphic curves, so equivalences between the three invariants known as
            %em GW/PT/GV correspondence
            are conjectured. But all of them use additional data:
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gromov-Witten+invariants"} Gromov-Witten invariants
            additionally use maps into the manifold, Pandharipande-Thomas invariants additionally use points on the curve (D0-D2-D6 bound states) and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gopakumar-Vafa+invariants"} Gopakumar-Vafa invariants
            additionally use
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            on the curve (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D2-branes"}> D2-branes
            ). As a result, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gromov-Witten+invariant"} Gromov-Witten invariant
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+number"} rational
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
          %h2#gwptgv_correspondence GW/PT/GV correspondence
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            be a three-dimensional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+manifold"} Calabi-Yau manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta\in H_2(M,\mathbb{Z})
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            class and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus"} genus
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudoholomorphic+curve"} pseudoholomorphic curve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} GW
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{GW}(g,\beta)\in\mathbb{Q}
            be the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gromov-Witten+invariant"} Gromov-Witten invariant
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} PT
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{PT}(g,\beta)\in\mathbb{Z}
            be the Pandharipande-Thomas invariant and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} GV
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{GV}(n,\beta)\in\mathbb{Z}
            be the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gopakumar-Vafa+invariant"} Gopakumar-Vafa invariant
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} GW
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mi β
                  %msup
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi g
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mn ∞
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} GV
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi β
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi k
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mn 2
                      %mi sin
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mi λ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi g
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mi β
                  %mo ;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sum_{g=0}^\infty\sum_{\beta\in H_2(M,\mathbb{Z})}\operatorname{GW}(g,\beta)q^{\beta}\lambda^{2g-2}
                  \=\sum_{k=1}^\infty\sum_{g=0}^\infty\sum_{\beta\in H_2(M,\mathbb{Z})}\frac{\operatorname{GV}(g,\beta)}{k}\left(2\sin\left(\frac{k\lambda}{2}\right)\right)^{2g-2}q^{k\beta};
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ln
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn ∞
                      %mn ∞
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi β
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi M
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mtext PT
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi q
                      %mi β
                    %msup
                      %mi λ
                      %mi n
                    %mo )
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mn ∞
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn ∞
                    %mn ∞
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} GV
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi β
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi λ
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mfrac
                          %mi k
                          %mn 2
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi λ
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mfrac
                          %mi k
                          %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi g
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mi β
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\ln\left(
                  1+\sum_{n=-\infty}^\infty\sum_{\beta\in H_2(M,\mathbb{Z})}\text{PT}(n,\beta)q^\beta\lambda^n
                  \\right)
                  \=\sum_{k=1}^\infty\sum_{n=-\infty}^\infty\sum_{\beta\in H_2(M,\mathbb{Z})}\frac{\operatorname{GV}(g,\beta)}{k}(-1)^{g-1}\left(
                  (-\lambda)^{\frac{k}{2}}-(-\lambda)^{\frac{k}{2}}
                  \\right)^{2g-2}q^{k\beta}.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#IonelParker99"}> Ionel &amp; Parker 99, Eq. (0.1)
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Toda21"} Toda 21, Eq. (7.2) &amp; Thrm. 7.1
